# Tuning GCC libraries to bsg_vanilla_2020 causes RTL error

- Source URL: https://github.com/bespoke-silicon-group/bsg_manycore/issues/586

While searching for performance last week, I noticed that the GCC libraries for manycore are not tuned for the vanilla core pipeline. 

To address this, I added `--with-tune=bsg_vanilla_2020` to software/riscv-tools/Makefile on line 139: 
```
		./configure --prefix=$(RISCV) --disable-linux --with-arch=$(TARGET_ARCH) --with-abi=$(TARGET_ABI) --disable-gdb --with-tune=bsg_vanilla_2020
```

(--with-tune is described here: [Link](https://gcc.gnu.org/install/configure.html))

The GCC toolchain seems to compile fine. It also seems to take the tuning flag correctly: 
